{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/753906-wod-setting-metro-manila","id":753906,"title":"WoD Setting - Metro Manila","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-04T06:59:24-08:00","id":753906,"title":"WoD Setting - Metro Manila","content":"To anyone on the forums who is Filipino and/or happens to live in the Metro Manila area, this is an open invitation for brainstorming ideas. I am looking for help in putting together stuff for a World of Darkness setting in Metro Manila. I have some stuff written up for a few of the supernatural lines, but I'll probably need help working out details and story hooks.<br /> <br /> So far, the references I have include the <i>Trese</i> series of comics, as well as what I remember from certain <i>teleseryes</i> like Encantadia (and its sequels), Sugo, and Aso ni San Roque, among other titles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T07:45:06-08:00","id":753994,"title":"","content":"I've been in there, but that was long ago and I didn't have much interest in the culture at the time nor did I really know that much as I did now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T08:22:58-08:00","id":754072,"title":"","content":"Flavor titles for some of the supernatural gamelines. Suggestions are welcome. <hr /><br /> <b>Vampire: The Requiem [The Black Pearl of the Orient]<br /> <br /> Werewolf: The Forsaken [Ang Huling Bantay]<br /> <br /> Promethean: The Created []<br /> <br /> Changeling: The Lost []<br /> <br /> Geist: The Sin-Eater []</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T16:33:41-07:00","id":964615,"title":"","content":"Hi Deionscribe, this comes almost a year late. Still looking for ideas? I'd love to help with the brainstorming. I run a Mage chronicle set in the consilium of Manila. The PCs are street-level mages who have been chasing Mysteries in Quiapo, Intramuros, Tondo, and Manila Bay.<br /> <br /> As the ST it's been fun and challenging 'Filipinizing' Mage concepts, and the players get to help in the world-building too. We've got a working lexicon, local mage history, and even videoke spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Let me know how I can help. Toying with the idea of a Changeling Manila setting next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T21:28:28-07:00","id":964767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/753906-wod-setting-metro-manila?p=964615#post964615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Deionscribe, this comes almost a year late. Still looking for ideas? I'd love to help with the brainstorming. I run a Mage chronicle set in the consilium of Manila. The PCs are street-level mages who have been chasing Mysteries in Quiapo, Intramuros, Tondo, and Manila Bay.<br /> <br /> As the ST it's been fun and challenging 'Filipinizing' Mage concepts, and the players get to help in the world-building too. We've got a working lexicon, local mage history, and even videoke spellcasting.<br /> <br /> Let me know how I can help. Toying with the idea of a Changeling Manila setting next.</div> </div> </div> </div>Better late than never <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Welcome aboard.<br /> <br /> Say, you mind sharing the stuff you got on Mage, so far? I'd be interested in seeing what you and your players have managed to put together. Not to mention I want to ask if you thought up any local Nameless Orders for your campaign.<br /> <br /> As for Changeling side of Manila (and the Philippines), I was thinking of having the Filipino Lost united in a manner similar to their Japanese counterparts. <i>Unlike</i> the Yosei, however, the Philippines' status as a former colonial power and a melting pot of different cultures has resulted in a Commonwealth of disparate Courts united under a fragile Bulwark of sorts. These Courts range from the Seasonal Courts (primarily the Monsoon and Dry Season variants from Winter Masques), the five Directional Courts, the Courts of Dawn and Dusk, and the few <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/938645-101-court-ideas?p=940155#post940155\">Courts of the Diwata</a> such as those of Maria Makiling.<br /> <br /> For terminology, I can see <i>Barangay</i> and <i>Barkada </i>having a different meaning in the context of the local Lost. The former could refer to an individual freehold, whereas the latter could be the equivalent of a motley?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 09-07-2016, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T07:28:50-07:00","id":964946,"title":"","content":"Thanks, and it's great seeing a fellow Manile\u00f1o on the forum too. So far, the Yosei Kingdom, is one of the most creative locales I've read. Plus points for basing it on a Japanese folktale. Can't see why a Manila Freehold would be any less interesting in its own way. Kudos on the Diwata Courts. Were you reading American Gods? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for Mage, our 'Fallen Manila Chronicles' involves <i>Mulat</i> who live, breathe, and practice sorcery in The Pearl, Manila's underground society for magic. The mtropolis' administrative body, the Camara is hopelessly mired in red tape and prone to the whims of large cabals. Rather than deal directly with threats, the Camara is in the habit of forming temporary cabals to perform ad hoc problem-solving. It's a noisy, disparate, chaotic, and utterly confusing place especially to foreign mages. Thankfully the locals are charming. The Pearl geographically encompasses parts of Metro Manila with a high concentration of Mulat who operate in the Estrada's Manila. Currently, the city has the lion's share of weirdness in the chronicle.<br /> <br /> There are scavenger spirits in Tondo which alternately feast on the despair and hope of the poor. In Intramuros, Space magic falters, and the district's ancient fortifications extend deep into the Shadow. In a forgotten Spanish prison, the PCs have encountered the ghosts of conquistadors. We don't have a central Mystery yet, but I'm partial to borrowing London's 'runewalking' in the 2e corebook. Our present antagonist is a celebrity feng shui master who seeks to return Manila to prosperity. Unfortunately that involves summoning an ancient pagan fertility god, and the PCs unite to stop him. It's not that simple though as the PCs have to resolve their conflicts with one another first.<br /> <br /> All the Orders are present, but localized. The Ilustrados represent the Silver Ladder, while the Maharlika share the warrior ethos of the Adamantine Arrow. Then you've got the Moriones (Guardians of the Veil), the Tanghalang Hiwaga (Mysterium), and the Sangguniang Malaya (Free Council). Historically, the first four were native Nameless Orders (roughly equivalent to the Maginoo, Maharlika, Timawa, and Alipin castes) before they disappeared during the Spanish conquest, and then resurfaced as a collection of Catholic devotional cults, masonic brotherhoods, and Enlightenment thinkers.<br /> <br /> As for Nameless, one of the PCs is a Nameless Obrimos who descends from a line of Ifugao tribal priests. I'm also in the early phase of developing 2 distinct Nameless Orders as future NPCs, one based in Binondo, the other based in the Muslim quarter of Quiapo. The world-building has been thorough, and I don't want to overwhelm. If you need specifics, I'd be happy to share more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4260,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","user":"terpsichordean","date":". 09-07-2016, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-07T08:42:14-07:00","id":964986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/753906-wod-setting-metro-manila?p=964946#post964946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, and it's great seeing a fellow Manile\u00f1o on the forum too.<br /> <br /> The world-building has been thorough, and I don't want to overwhelm. If you need specifics, I'd be happy to share more. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The feeling's mutual xD And no, I never read American Gods. My primary inspirations are noted down on the OP. As for a central Mystery, I would consider tying it to ley lines and/or the high abundance of Hallows and Verges. Just as its geographical position leaves it open to natural disasters, perhaps the Philippines is also a potent nexus for Supernal energy. Heck, maybe Supernal Entities could remain in the Fallen World a lot longer than usual to emphasize this.<br /> <br /> As for the Diwata Courts, the only one I've got worked out for building up details on is the one for Maria Makiling. I'm probably going to wait until Lost 2E is out before I start putting it together, but I was wondering if the Metro Manila area is predominantly under the Seasonal and Directional Courts whereas those of the Diwatas (while they are present in numbers in the cities) have a bigger presence out in the rural provinces.<br /> <br /> As for that pagan fertility god, might I offer a suggestion for prepping for a Changeling chronicle? Perhaps said god could be some sort of powerful fae entity? A high Wyrd and low Clarity changeling at the least, and a Huntsman or an exiled True Fae at most?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 09-07-2016, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T20:36:58-07:00","id":966017,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Changelings with ties to Filipino-Chinese enclaves (Binondo, Banawe, San Juan) adhere to Directional Courts? Elsewhere, alternative courts might include:<br /> <br /> Myths<br /> Maria Makiling could be a Court or it could be a title held ala Tokyo's Moon Princess. Imagine a Freehold of Los Ba\u00f1os based around Mt. Makiling, UPLB, the Makiling School for the Arts, and IRRI, each loosely represented by a court.<br /> <br /> Festivals<br /> Filipinos mark the calendar around certain holidays, creating cultural milieu over time. What might the Court of Passion (Kwaresma), or the Court of Jubilation (Pasko) look like? One can even dig into things like La Naval, Edsa anniversary, and the UP Lantern Parade.<br /> <br /> Materials<br /> The Court of Ivory Fingers harks back to old arts of carving Catholic imagery in expensive ivory, feeding on the collective piety and religious pageantry of Filipinos. What might the Courts of Acacia, Capiz, and Brass look like?<br /> <br /> For Mage, I appreciate the suggestion regarding Verges and Hallows. That could tie-in with rune-walking. Perhaps the rapid pace of construction in the Metropolis is disrupting the old 'routes'? I can already see a land developer blocking roads or seizing old property serve as the front for the Seers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-08T21:18:54-07:00","id":966030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/753906-wod-setting-metro-manila?p=966017#post966017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Mage, I appreciate the suggestion regarding Verges and Hallows. That could tie-in with rune-walking. Perhaps the rapid pace of construction in the Metropolis is disrupting the old 'routes'? I can already see a land developer blocking roads or seizing old property serve as the front for the Seers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. And to differentiate it from London, perhaps said disruption might have consequences not forseen by even the Seers. I had this idea that Ondoy was partly the work of a Bound whose prison was breached over time.<br /> <br /> For Changeling, I can agree that the Chinese enclaves would establish Directional Courts. And those other ideas are pretty interesting too. Making the Court/s of Maria Makiling be a freehold similar to the Yosei Kingdom, in particular, is a good alternative to the Dreamer patron concept I had.<br /> <br /> On an unrelated note, what are your thoughts on the spirit of the Pasig River having been twisted into a <i>magath</i> as a result of pollution?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T10:49:17-07:00","id":966324,"title":"","content":"We haven't touched anything related to the Pasig yet, but I imagine the spirit of Pasig River as an ancient crocodilian. Perhaps decades of pollution has shrunk the spirit or shriveled it to scales and bones, a scavenger of sorts.<br /> <br /> Here's a bare bones writeup I did for a future Changeling 2e set in Manila:<br /> <br /> Overview<br /> The Republic of Perlandia is all that stands in the way between Manila's Lost and the incursions of the Magino-o. Founded in the ashes of the Second World War, it's aim was to represent a united front against Arcadia while providing a safe refuge for Engkantos.<br /> <br /> Perlandia is also the home of Manila's Monsoon Courts: the aspiring Amihan and the fatalistic Habagat. Each reigns for their season, tied to the various holidays and festivals of the metropolis, before passing authority to the other - a notion which utterly confounds the despotic Gentry. This alliance however hasn't always been so clean-cut; rivalry is commonplace as both parties seek to curry popular support with the Freehold's masses.<br /> <br /> The Amihan, Court of the Northeastern Wind<br /> Passionate and festive, the Amihan hold sway during Manila's 'dry' season beginning with the last months of the year up until the blazing heights of summer. Marked by fair weather and little rain, it is a season of rituals and revolutions when processions, festivals, and vigils rally together communities.<br /> <br /> Many in the sun court share a deterministic view of life, believing that great things can only be accomplished through acts of courage and sacrifice. Steeled by their durance and fueled by dreams of a better future, their leaders view themselves as the example other Engkantos should follow. Thus, both the political martyr and the charismatic sun king are twin aspects of the Amihan's peculiar attempt at servant-leadership.<br /> <br /> Through strength in arms and honey-tongued eloquence, Amihan courtiers mean to foment the masses; to inspire every Lost to battle the forces of Arcadia head on, and in the daylight.<br /> <br /> Popular Festivals: Christmas, New Year, Chinese New Year, EDSA Revolution, Holy Week, Labor Day<br /> <br /> Common attire: Bright, festive patterns, sun medallions, sunglassess, pins with feathers, sun tattoos<br /> <br /> Habagat, The Court of the Southwestern Wind<br /> As the sweltering heat ripens to tropical humidity, the mysterious Habagat take over the reigns of Perlandia. Their ascension is accompanied by heavy rains and the country's notorious 'typhoon season'. Floods rise to reclaim parts of the swollen metropolis, while the public looks to omens and signs; dread, anticipation, and inner resiliency.<br /> <br /> Fatalism is deeply rooted in the Storm Court's philosophy. What good can one ultimately do against the brutal elements or the fickle cruelty of the Magino-o? Not that the Habagat will stand helpless. As leaders they are hard-nosed pragmatists who make tough decisions based on realpolitik. Some find Storm courtiers too jaded but the Habagat know better than to openly tempt the Fae with brash action.<br /> <br /> Many Habagat Engkantos find a use as spies, saboteurs, and scholars - anything to pry secrets from Arcadia. For Perlandia to weather the coming storms, its citizens must be willing to commit anything and everything.<br /> <br /> Popular Occasions: Beginning of classes, Philippine Independence Day, National Heroes Day, All Saints and Souls Days, La Naval<br /> <br /> Common attire: Dark or subdued colors, deep hues, Shield medallions, umbrellas, scarves or shawls, raincoats and hoodies","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T22:26:04-07:00","id":966628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/753906-wod-setting-metro-manila?p=966324#post966324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We haven't touched anything related to the Pasig yet, but I imagine the spirit of Pasig River as an ancient crocodilian. Perhaps decades of pollution has shrunk the spirit or shriveled it to scales and bones, a scavenger of sorts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. That works. My version of the spirit was more along the lines of a humanoid elemental, one that has been twisted into a magath like Irinam.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>terpsichordean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/753906-wod-setting-metro-manila?p=966324#post966324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's a bare bones writeup I did for a future Changeling 2e set in Manila:</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey xD I've been trying to work out the Monsoon Courts for a while, now. Great work. Their theme is sort of like a seasonal variant of the Dusk and Dawn Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:33:00-07:00","id":971267,"title":"","content":"Cool, let me know how that works out for you! If it's Mage you're looking to explore, just let me know. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T15:59:56-07:00","id":977443,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4260_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4260\" data-vbnamecard=\"4260\">terpsichordean</a> <br /> <br /> Say, could I have a second opinion on these write-ups for your Courts' Mantles? I got curious enough with the idea to make a rough draft.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <b>Court of Amihan</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 -- The Mantle may manifest as a warm breeze or the feeling of sunlight on one's skin. Gain a dot in Empathy.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 -- Courtiers gain a dot in a Goblin Vow related to the Court.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 -- Courtiers gain two dots in the Indomitable Merit as their Mantle's warm winds renew their determination.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 -- Courtiers gain a Personal Approach related to how they fulfill the ideals and story of the court. Huntsmen cannot gain Yearning from a Court Approach unless they fulfill the Personal Approach first.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 -- Courtiers gain the Inspiring Merit as their very presence lifts the spirits of their peers<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Court of Habagat</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 -- The Mantle may appear as faint bursts of electricity, or sudden chills in the air. All rolls made to intimidate the changeling suffer a -1 penalty.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 -- Courtiers gain a dot in a Goblin Vow related to the Court.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 -- Courtiers gain two dots in the Meditative Mind Merit as the violent winds of their Mantle sharpen their minds.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 -- Courtiers gain a Personal Approach related to how they fulfill the ideals and story of the court. Huntsmen cannot gain Yearning from a Court Approach unless they fulfill the Personal Approach first.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 -- Courtiers gain three dots in the Hardy Merit as their bodies harden against the coming storm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":8180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","user":"Deionscribe","date":". 11-05-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}